The source-attribution diagnosis remains a hypothesis. The latest measured algorithm changed the multi-selection wrapper despite unchanged standard arithmetic and percentile-sort semantics. Recorded unchanged baseline/original controls also varied between windows. The +37.9967% all-percentile ratio of medians, +6.0910% median paired percentage, five of seven slower pairs and overlapping ranges remain unmodified. They do not establish a causal compiler or wrapper effect. The complete86-file correctness inventory plus its manifest and complete2217-file measured-review inventory plus its manifest are preserved as2305 inert snapshots, including all current/historical failures, source, raw logs, figures and disclosures. There is no rebinding of old observations to this candidate.

Root's current request fixes the faithful three-role protocol: authenticated original @grafana/data13.2.3 with actual Lodash4.17.23, exact application baseline, and this wrapper candidate. This supersedes the earlier diagnosis document's proposed four-role diagnostic as the current measurement design; that proposal remains inert history. There are seven fixed workloads, seven repetitions and three roles,147 sequential children per separate sequence, with the same rotating role orders as before. Original and baseline controls share the new window with candidate; comparisons against the old mixed candidate remain descriptive cross-window history and cannot establish causation.

The seven specification objects, seeds, generator/canonical source digests,14 input/expected files, fresh result/cache graphs, complete-cache rereads, subset-cache rereads and registry metadata hash remain exact. Small standard, large standard, single p95, all99 percentiles, all124 calculations, constructed p95 and organ-pipe p95 are never substituted or filtered. The66-input additional fixture is correctness provenance only. Existing warmups, iterations, transient blocks and retained counts remain unchanged, including the short two-warmup/three-iteration multi-selection cases. No posthoc acceptance threshold is introduced. An additional warmup/dispatch/module-layout or profiler diagnostic needs its own prospective design and authorization; it cannot replace these seven workloads.

Timing retains the tested old measured loop and lifecycle. Each timing child loads all three implementations for common metadata and fresh/cache correctness prevalidation, then times only the selected implementation. Its memory/CPU diagnostics are not an isolated memory comparison. Bounds remain60 seconds per child,2MiB child capture,600 seconds outer timing controller and4MiB outer capture. Preserve every raw/partial/failure row and every median, min/max range, overlapping range and signed paired candidate-minus-baseline/original difference. Observed ranges are descriptive, not confidence intervals. A failed branch aborts remaining children; no silent retry or selection of a best case.

Memory is a distinct fresh quiet window, not authorized by timing completion. Each fresh memory child loads exactly one implementation: original six actual CJS files, baseline one ESM module, candidate two ESM modules. The source-validated numeric-PID observer must deliver a matching PID sample before the parent sends start. Nominal polling is100ms. There is no process-start identity proof or atomic PID-reuse/process-tree protection. Existing bounds stay120 seconds per child,256MiB old-space,512MiB polled/checkpoint RSS and4MiB captured child/observer output. The controller has no outer watchdog. Timers, observation and logical RSS limits do not promise an instantaneous OS memory sandbox or bounded cumulative allocation. Partial, failed, killed or limit-hit trials stay visible and censored.

Keep lifetime peak RSS, observer maximum and checkpoint RSS separate. Initialization, shared input, warm base, transient, retained and released checkpoints stay distinct. Retained-minus-beforeRetention and released-minus-warmBase are the prospective diagnostics; additionally retain released-minus-beforeRetention for historical comparison when consolidating. Every signed negative child value and paired difference stays visible. A zero control permits a signed difference but no percentage; unavailable percentages remain null. Common serializer pressure and complete/subset cache rereads occur after retained snapshots and before release, so GC/allocator and temporary-validation effects remain included. Release observations do not prove leaks or allocation superiority.

Only correctness-only harness preflights execute during readiness: synthetic signed/censoring summaries, invalid timestamp guards, source/import-graph checks, observer syntax parsing and one fresh result plus two cached rereads per fixed input per role. Memory check-only executes three children with exactly one implementation each; it performs no warmup/transient/retention loops, snapshots or observer run. Timing check-only authenticates63 packets across all three roles with no timed loop. The already frozen full/held-out/cache/alias/dispatch correctness campaign is reused as finite provenance, not replayed as a new independent corpus during readiness.

